   "page_end": "422",
   "note": "Two questions in a row, as in أئذا كنا ترابا أئنا: eleven places in all (al-Raʿd, two in al-Isrāʾ, al-Muʾminūn, al-Naml, al-ʿAnkabūt, al-Sajda, two in al-Ṣāffāt, al-Wāqiʿa, al-Nāziʿāt). The book adds the manner: Nāfiʿ and Ruways make the question with a hamza and a softened one, and Qālūn puts an alif between; al-Kisāʾī and Rawḥ read two hamzas; Ibn Kathīr does not lengthen and Abū ʿAmr does; Hishām puts an alif between the two and Ibn Dhakwān does not; Abū Jaʿfar softens the second and puts an alif between. The places where a reader departs from this are the next entries.",
   "chapter": "الاستفهامان المتتاليان"
  },
